@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# Kombatant Effects
+
+Open Kombatant > Effects / GShade presets, or use the Effects button in Studio.
+
+Native effects use the viewer renderer: exposure, CAS sharpening, AO,
+depth of field, and new saturation/contrast/vignette grading. Color grading has
+its own bypass. Restore returns all native controls to their values at panel open.
+
+The Windows package builds and includes ReShade from source, revision
+7bf9de8b33bcc76c3177007e65d73c72dd0f34c0 (BSD-3-Clause).
+It loads as KombatantFX64.dll before OpenGL context creation, using ReShade's
+normal OpenGL hook path. The viewer registers an API add-on to control presets
+and the overlay. No GShade binary is bundled, and GShade is not rebranded here.
+
+Enable shader effects, enter the full path to an existing .ini file and choose
+Load .ini, or choose Shader controls / browse presets. Home toggles the overlay.
+Use its standard preset browser, technique list, sliders, save, and screenshot
+controls. The shipped neutral sample is an executable shader compatibility test.
+
+Copy your matching .fx/.fxh shader files to reshade-shaders/Shaders and their
+textures to reshade-shaders/Textures beside the viewer executable. Keep any
+required folder structure. Add other search paths in the overlay Settings tab.
+An .ini does not include shader code. ReShade-compatible GShade shaders can run;
+GShade-only extensions, missing shaders, and version-specific uniforms can fail.
+Read the overlay compilation diagnostics. Do not treat a loaded preset as proof
+that every technique compiled. Shader licenses govern any packs you add.
+
+MXAO and other depth effects need a valid depth buffer; configure Generic Depth
+in the overlay if necessary. SL's deferred renderer uses intermediate framebuffers,
+so depth-buffer compatibility still needs Windows in-world verification. Native
+AO and depth of field remain available independently. Runtime effects process
+the final window including UI. Use ReShade screenshots for shader-processed
+images; the viewer's internal high-resolution snapshots run before presentation.
+
+Effects start disabled for each session and after OpenGL context recreation.
+Reopen this panel and enable them after a context reset. If another opengl32.dll
+exists beside the viewer, built-in FX stays off to avoid stacking two injectors.
+Keep only the viewer's supplied runtime DLL. KOMBATANT_DISABLE_FX=1 disables
+loading it for recovery; native controls still work. It stays loaded until exit
+because unloading active OpenGL hooks is unsafe.
+
+Build from the applied viewer sources: run powershell -File kombatant/build-fx.ps1
+before compiling the viewer, then run it with -StageOnly after compiling. The
+GitHub workflow performs both steps and stages the DLL, sample, and license.
+Windows compilation, an actual GL session, resizing/fullscreen changes, shader
+compilation, and representative user presets must pass before claiming release
+quality or complete GShade compatibility.
diff --git a/kombatant/README.md b/kombatant/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..81e722e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/kombatant/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@
+# Kombatant Viewer — source preview 0.3
+
+A native C++ Second Life viewer customization based on NiranV/Black-Dragon-Viewer,
+upstream commit b2ca434b39bcd93aff0e23414999dddd73527e05.
+
+STATUS: Source preview. Not a compiled viewer, installer, or tested release.
+
+## What is implemented
+
+- Kombatant application title, build channel and top-level menu.
+- Separate KombatantViewer user settings directory, preserving the installed
+  Black Dragon profile. Upstream internal executable/project names remain.
+- A native Studio panel at Kombatant > Kombatant Studio, with three modes:
+
+| Setting | Everyday | Cinematic | Crowded Area |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Draw distance | 96 m | 128 m | 64 m |
+| Shadows | Sun/moon | Sun/moon + projectors | Off |
+| Ambient occlusion | On | On | Off |
+| Probe detail | Static | Static + dynamic | Static |
+| Full-detail avatar limit | 8 | 12 | 4 |
+| Avatar complexity limit | 150,000 | 250,000 | 100,000 |
+| Glow | Not modified | Not modified | Not modified |
+
+Both picture modes use the existing Khronos Neutral tone mapper. Cinematic adds
+subtle vignette. Chromatic aberration is disabled. Depth of field starts off and
+is available as an optional toggle. Existing region lighting and materials still
+control the scene's appearance. These are renderer settings, not a new renderer.
+
+The panel has Ambient Occlusion and Depth of Field toggles, access to full
+Preferences, and a Restore Previous Settings button. Restore captures only the
+settings changed by a mode, immediately before the first mode switch. It remains
+available during this viewer session, not after restarting. Normal viewer
+preferences persistence applies on clean exit. No settings change just by opening
+Studio. To return to the original profile, use Restore before exiting.
+
+This first UI pass adds Studio and branding; the rest of the interface remains
+Black Dragon. Crowded Area can simplify or hide complex avatars. Performance is
+not benchmarked. No DLSS, ray tracing, frame generation or fixed FPS claim.
+
+## Build on Windows 11 x64
+
+Required: Visual Studio 2022 C++ desktop workload and Windows SDK, CMake, Git/Git
+Bash, Python 3.11 with `autobuild` and `llsd`, and access to the upstream binary
+dependency download servers. The bundled autobuild.xml owns library versions.
+Install Python tooling with `python -m pip install autobuild llsd`.
+
+Open an x64 VS developer environment, launch Git Bash inheriting it, and run:
+
+```bash
+bash kombatant/build-windows.sh
+```
+
+The script selects ReleaseOS, OpenAL audio, no KDU, no proprietary build mode,
+no upstream crash-report database, and no installer packaging. This script has
+been shell-syntax checked only. The upstream dependencies and actual Windows
+compile/link still need verification. Media, voice and audio also need runtime
+checks. The existing GitHub build workflow is upstream's workflow and is not a
+validated Kombatant release pipeline.
+
+## Validation completed here
+
+- All changed XUI files parse as XML.
+- All 15 mode setting names resolve in upstream settings definitions, with
+  compatible scalar/vector types.
+- Native floater registration, menu callback, resource inclusion pattern checked.
+- Patch whitespace and build-script shell syntax checked.
+
+Windows build, login, rendering, UI layout, voice, inventory, uploads, snapshots,
+multiple launches and FPS/VRAM measurements are NOT tested. This Linux environment
+has no Windows compiler or graphics session, so no executable was produced.
+
+## Runtime acceptance before release
+
+1. Compile and link ReleaseOS on Windows; confirm the new Studio resource ships.
+2. Launch without touching Black Dragon's settings directory.
+3. Open Studio, switch every mode, close/reopen Studio, and verify Restore.
+4. Compare rendered scenes in the same region with the same camera, environment,
+   avatars and resolution. Record FPS, frame time and VRAM in all three modes.
+5. Check PBR materials, projectors, AO, vignette and optional depth of field.
+6. Check login, inventory, chat, voice, audio, media, uploads, snapshots and exit.
+7. Review packaging identifiers, icons, installer behavior and third-party viewer
+   distribution requirements before publishing. Preserve upstream attribution.
+
+## Licensing
+
+The upstream LICENSE and source notices are retained. New Studio code is
+LGPL-2.1-only. Retain notices and dependency licenses with any distribution.
+This project is a separate customization and is not an official Black Dragon
+or Linden Lab release.
+
+## 12K photo output (0.2)
+
+The Save to Disk snapshot dropdown now offers 12,288 x 6,912 (16:9),
+84,934,656 pixels. Upstream's 11,520 x 6,480 option labeled 12K is replaced.
+The snapshot dimension cap and unlocked width/height controls are aligned at
+12,288. Studio has a snapshot button and brief instructions.
+
+After building: open Studio > Open snapshots / 12K photos, select Save to Disk,
+enable Allow High Resolutions, disable inclusion of UI and HUD, then choose
+12288x6912 (12K). Select PNG and refresh the snapshot before saving. For this
+16:9 preset, disable Constrain proportions if the window has a different aspect
+ratio. The renderer's existing allocation checks and tiled fallback remain.
+
+12K is saved-image resolution; gameplay rendering stays at window resolution.
+Photo detail remains limited by loaded textures, meshes, lighting and the
+existing renderer. No AI upscaling or texture reconstruction was added. A single
+RGB output buffer is about 243 MiB; render targets, encoding and previews need
+additional memory. Successful capture, exact saved dimensions, seams and visual
+quality still require Windows runtime testing. No 12K runtime image was produced
+in this environment.
+
+## Experimental live 12K rendering (0.3)
+
+Studio now has a Live World Rendering selector: Window / 4K / 8K / 12K.
+This controls main-world offscreen render target width, not snapshot resolution.
+At a 16:9 viewport, 12K requests 12,288 x 6,912 pixels every frame. Other window
+shapes preserve their own aspect ratio. The final world image is sampled to the
+physical window; the monitor does not gain pixels and UI remains window-sized.
+
+The main render allocation and resize comparison share the same size calculation.
+Scaling is applied once, fixing upstream's repeated scaling on resize. Reflection
+probe buffers retain their upstream scale. Explicit snapshot sizes normally bypass
+the live-width override unless they match the world viewport's input dimensions.
+GPU texture, renderbuffer and viewport limits are checked. An unsupported request
+or allocation fallback disables the live override to avoid repeated allocation
+attempts. This does not guarantee protection against driver hangs or every memory
+failure in upstream's renderer. The control resets to Window on application restart.
+The Studio Actual World Buffer readout reports the allocated screen target size,
+rather than repeating the selected label. Existing resolution divisor/multiplier
+settings apply again when the live override is disabled.
+
+12K at 16:9 shades 84,934,656 pixels each frame, about 41 times 1080p. Deferred HDR,
+depth and postprocessing targets can consume several GiB beyond scene textures.
+This is an experimental source implementation, not a validated 12K gameplay build
+or a promise of good FPS on any GPU. No Windows compile or live GPU test was
+possible here. Validate allocation, scene/depth alignment, picking, UI composition,
+resizing, all postprocessing, reflection passes and FPS before using it routinely.
+
+Source validation: changed settings/XUI parse as XML; settings are declared and
+connected to the resize callback; selector widths and aspect calculations checked;
+patch whitespace and Windows helper shell syntax checked. Windows runtime tests
+and exact GPU output remain unverified.
+
+## GitHub Actions compile attempt
+
+The manual `Kombatant Windows build` workflow uses a Windows 2022 runner,
+Visual Studio x64 environment, and the existing ReleaseOS helper. It uploads
+compiler logs even on failure and the Release output directory on success.
+It does not publish a release or installer. These outputs have not been
+validated as a complete portable application. The workflow has not been run.
diff --git a/kombatant/build-fx.ps1 b/kombatant/build-fx.ps1
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d57fd58
--- /dev/null
+++ b/kombatant/build-fx.ps1
@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+param([switch]$StageOnly)
+$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
+$root = Split-Path $PSScriptRoot -Parent
+$source = Join-Path $root 'indra/third_party/reshade'
+$revision = '7bf9de8b33bcc76c3177007e65d73c72dd0f34c0'
+function Check-Native { if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "Command failed with exit code $LASTEXITCODE" } }
+if (!$StageOnly) {
+    if (!(Test-Path "$source/.git")) {
+        git clone --no-checkout https://github.com/crosire/reshade.git $source
+        Check-Native
+    }
+    git -C $source checkout --detach $revision
+    Check-Native
+    git -C $source submodule update --init --recursive
+    Check-Native
+    if ((git -C $source rev-parse HEAD) -ne $revision) { throw 'Unexpected ReShade revision' }
+    $vswhere = "${env:ProgramFiles(x86)}/Microsoft Visual Studio/Installer/vswhere.exe"
+    $msbuild = & $vswhere -latest -products '*' -requires Microsoft.Component.MSBuild -find 'MSBuild/**/Bin/MSBuild.exe' | Select-Object -First 1
+    if (!$msbuild) { throw 'Visual Studio MSBuild is required' }
+    & $msbuild "$source/ReShade.sln" /t:ReShade /m:2 /p:Configuration=Release '/p:Platform=64-bit' /verbosity:minimal
+    Check-Native
+} else {
+    $output = Join-Path $root 'build-vc170-64/newview/Release'
+    if (!(Test-Path $output)) { throw 'Viewer output directory missing' }
+    # Unpackaged builds omit runtime resources from viewer_manifest's copy action.
+    foreach ($directory in @('app_settings', 'skins', 'character')) {
+        Copy-Item "$root/indra/newview/$directory" $output -Recurse -Force
+    }
+    $packages = Join-Path $root 'build-vc170-64/packages'
+    if (!(Test-Path "$packages/fonts")) { throw 'Viewer font package missing' }
+    Copy-Item "$packages/fonts" $output -Recurse -Force
+    if (Test-Path "$packages/dictionaries") {
+        Copy-Item "$packages/dictionaries" "$output/app_settings" -Recurse -Force
+    }
+    foreach ($required in @('app_settings/settings.xml', 'app_settings/settings_blackdragon.xml',
+        'app_settings/shaders/class1/deferred/postDeferredGammaCorrect.glsl',
+        'skins/default/xui/en/floater_kombatant_effects.xml', 'character/avatar_lad.xml')) {
+        if (!(Test-Path (Join-Path $output $required))) { throw "Missing portable resource: $required" }
+    }
+    if (!(Get-ChildItem "$output/fonts/*.ttf")) { throw 'No fonts in portable package' }
+
+    Copy-Item "$source/bin/x64/Release/ReShade64.dll" "$output/KombatantFX64.dll"
+    Copy-Item "$source/LICENSE.md" "$output/ReShade-LICENSE.md"
+    $notices = Join-Path $output 'ReShade-licenses'
+    Get-ChildItem "$source/deps" -Recurse -File | Where-Object { $_.Name -match '^(LICENSE|COPYING|NOTICE)' } | ForEach-Object {
+        $relative = $_.FullName.Substring($source.Length + 1)
+        $destination = Join-Path $notices $relative
+        New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force (Split-Path $destination -Parent) | Out-Null
+        Copy-Item $_.FullName $destination
+    }
+    # Do not overwrite an existing user's configuration or preset.
+    if (!(Test-Path "$output/ReShade.ini")) { Copy-Item "$PSScriptRoot/fx/ReShade.ini" $output }
+    if (!(Test-Path "$output/KombatantDefault.ini")) { Copy-Item "$PSScriptRoot/fx/KombatantDefault.ini" $output }
+    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force "$output/reshade-shaders/Shaders", "$output/reshade-shaders/Textures" | Out-Null
+    Copy-Item "$PSScriptRoot/fx/KombatantColor.fx" "$output/reshade-shaders/Shaders/"
+    Copy-Item "$PSScriptRoot/FX-README.md" $output
+    if (!(Test-Path "$output/KombatantFX64.dll")) { throw 'Runtime staging failed' }
+}
